# Normalize all text files to LF in the repo, and check them out as LF on every
# platform (Windows included). One line-ending everywhere = no CRLF/LF churn.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts MUST be LF — a CRLF entrypoint.sh breaks the shebang inside the
# Linux Docker container.
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts stay CRLF (none today, but future-proofed).
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf

# Treat these as binary so Git never touches their bytes.
*.exe   binary
*.gif   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# web/dist is the built SPA (webui/ -> web/dist). It is committed on purpose — the Go
# binary embeds it and `go build` must work without a Node toolchain — but it is
# generated output, not source, and it should never be read as a change someone wrote.
#
# linguist-generated collapses it by default in GitHub diffs and keeps it out of the
# language stats; -diff on assets/ stops `git diff` printing a 300 kB minified bundle
# over the change that actually needs reviewing. web/dist/index.html keeps its normal
# diff: it is four readable lines, and the hashed filenames it points at are the quickest
# confirmation that the bundle was rebuilt.
web/dist/**             linguist-generated=true
web/dist/assets/**      -diff
